{
  "_comment": "Domains whose reporting is credible enough to cite as open-web (web-search) evidence. This is source SELECTION, not verdict determination: source risk stays about the publisher and never makes a claim false (app/verdict/engine.py rule 6). Entries are bare hosts - no scheme, www or path - and a listed host covers its subdomains. The core government, education and international suffixes (gov, mil, int, edu, gov.in, nic.in, ac.in, ac.uk, gov.uk, edu.au, gov.au, edu.pk) are trusted in app/sources/credibility.py and are not repeated here. user_content_paths names sections of listed hosts that anyone can post to; pages there are not citable. Every host was resolved and fetched when added - on 2026-09-17, and sports_news on 2026-09-24 - and served the named organisation (or a bot wall in front of it). This is data: grow it, and tests/unit/test_credibility.py keeps its shape honest.",
  "_verified": "2026-09-17",
  "_criteria": {
    "sources": [
      "IFCN verified signatories: the list IFCN publishes at github.com/IFCN/verified-signatories (2026-09-01 update) and that file's history back to 2018",
      "EFCSN verified members: members.efcsn.com/signatories",
      "Ownership: Media Ownership Monitor India, Wikipedia, ThePrint, The Caravan and Newslaundry reporting",
      "EU DisinfoLab: 'Indian Chronicles' (2020) and '#BadSources' on ANI",
      "Freedom House, Freedom in the World country ratings"
    ],
    "included": [
      "Fact-checkers currently verified by IFCN or EFCSN.",
      "Fact-checkers IFCN verified in the past (per its published list history) whose domain still serves the same organisation - listed apart, in fact_checkers_formerly_verified, because accreditation lapses on renewal cycles and many reputable checkers are between renewals.",
      "News organisations whose fact-check desks are IFCN or EFCSN verified are listed under their news category, not as fact-checkers.",
      "Wire services and public-service broadcasters.",
      "Established newspapers of record and quality news publications with a public editorial team.",
      "International organisations, health and science authorities, peer-reviewed publishers, and disinformation-research organisations.",
      "Second-level domains whose registration is restricted to governments or accredited academic institutions, in countries rated Free or Partly Free by Freedom House."
    ],
    "not_included": [
      "Outlets owned or controlled by a serving elected representative or party office-holder, or their immediate family; party and religious-organisation organs.",
      "State propaganda outlets (e.g. Xinhua, CGTN, Global Times, TASS, RT, Press TV, KCNA) and government-aligned outlets in countries rated Not Free.",
      "Outlets documented citing fabricated sources - ANI (Asian News International), per EU DisinfoLab - and tabloids.",
      "Publishers with documented peer-review quality concerns or mass retractions, and preprint servers (arXiv, medRxiv, bioRxiv, SSRN, Research Square), which are not peer reviewed.",
      "Open user-submission platforms (Medium, Substack, Quora, Reddit, ResearchGate, academia.edu) and the open sections of listed hosts, via user_content_paths.",
      "Defunct organisations and domains that now serve something else."
    ]
  },
